course: dictionary
lesson: 1254
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Burgundy can be a colour, a place, or a kind of wine. Read the words around it and ask: which meaning fits here?
explain: «She wore a burgundy scarf to school.» A scarf is clothing, and clothes are often described by colour, so burgundy is the colour: a dark purplish-red, like red wine. Check by swapping in another colour, such as «a dark red scarf», and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Now read this: «France grew by absorbing great territories such as Burgundy and Brittany.» Territories are lands, so here Burgundy is a place, a region in eastern France. A capital B is another clue that it is a name, not a colour.
explain: Capital letters often help. Burgundy with a capital B is usually a place or a name in history. Burgundy with a small b is usually the colour. Still, always check the sentence, because the words around the word are the best clue.
fact: Burgundy is a dark purplish-red colour, like red wine.
fact: Burgundy is also a region in eastern France, famous for its wine.
fact: Wine from Burgundy can be red or white.
fact: In history, the Dukes of Burgundy were powerful in the Middle Ages.
fact: In French, the region is called «Bourgogne».
exercise: «The bride wore a burgundy dress.» What colour is the dress? | *Dark purplish-red | Bright green | Bright yellow | Pale blue
exercise: «France grew by absorbing great territories such as Burgundy and Brittany.» Here Burgundy is a... | *A region in France | A kind of cheese | A school subject | A colour
exercise: In «France grew by absorbing great territories such as Burgundy and Brittany», which word tells you Burgundy is a land? | *territories | absorbing | grew | France
test: Jo bought a bottle of white burgundy for the dinner party. What kind of burgundy is it? | A town in Scotland | *Wine from Burgundy | A type of dress | A dark red colour
test: Which sentence uses burgundy as a colour? | The Dukes of Burgundy were powerful in the Middle Ages. | Burgundy is a region in eastern France. | *Her school jumper was burgundy. | The French call the region Bourgogne.
exam: Burgundy can mean a colour, a place or a wine; how do you pick the right meaning? | Guess the first meaning you think of | Ask your teacher every single time | *Read the words around it and swap each meaning in to see which one fits | Skip the word and never come back to it
